1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,600
You can't run away from it, because you have already seen the light.

2
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,840
Oh my gosh, the girls are going to flock to him like geese.

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,520
Hey, cut it out.

4
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:21,400
What would you do if this gets you a bunch of new fans?

5
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,640
Like that would ever happen to me.

6
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:25,960
You can never be sure.

7
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,820
Think you got what it takes when the time comes?

8
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:31,280
Sorry, there's someone else I like.

9
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:35,740
Huh? What? What are you talking about?

10
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,980
She wasn't there, was she?

11
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,720
Sorry, there's someone else I like a lot.

12
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:44,680
Let's practice. I like you, Ichikawa.

13
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,360
Come on.

14
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:58,060
Yamada... likes me?

15
00:00:58,820 --> 00:00:59,660
Huh?

16
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,820
Even if she does, that doesn't mean anything's changed.

17
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:08,840
It actually means I gotta be more careful.

18
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:12,080
Unlike when someone doesn't like you at all,

19
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:15,280
messing up when someone actually does ruins things for good.

20
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:16,920
Watch yourself.

21
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:18,080
Ah, just stop it!

22
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,720
You can't go getting creepy.

23
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,720
Hey, uh...

24
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,200
Oh, yeah.

25
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:28,600
The basketball club is gonna go out to do karaoke with everyone who just graduated.

26
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,320
You coming?

27
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,380
What? Of course I'll come!

28
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,080
Hard to find the right timing to talk.

29
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:36,200
Not much I can do about that.

30
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:40,760
Karaoke, huh?

31
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,200
Not the sort of thing I ever do.

32
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,660
Yamada's coming too!

33
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:47,780
No way, really?

34
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:48,320
Yeah!

35
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,760
It's the basketball club!

36
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,840
The B-Ball guys are going too?

37
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:55,600
Whoever's going straight there, follow me!

38
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:18,260
Don't be creepy like this!

39
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:19,160
Yay!

40
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:30,700
Okay, Yamada, you're up next.

41
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,780
Are you still eating?

42
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:36,020
No worries, we'll do another toast.

43
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,700
Everyone pick up your glasses.

44
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:41,240
Then here's to Kobayashi's amazing three-point shot.

45
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,080
Hooray!

46
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,760
Okay, Yamada, now you.

47
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:48,420
She's always eating!

48
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:52,800
There they are.

49
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,300
Closer than I thought!

50
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,520
Better watch myself.

51
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,140
Who wanted melon soda again?

52
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:58,480
Huh?

53
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:00,320
Isn't that...

54
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,380
That's the kid who gave the farewell speech.

55
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,520
Yeah, you're right.

56
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,420
Everyone has been talking about you.

57
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,080
Did you ad-lib that whole thing?

58
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,260
Hey, come on, sing with us!

59
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,560
Go on already.

60
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:16,960
Ichikawa!

61
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:17,880
Yeah!

62
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,520
What are you doing here?

63
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:21,320
Huh?

64
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,740
I'm so dead.

65
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:33,420
I'm just some creep stalking her in her fun little party.

66
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:35,520
I'm...

67
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:49,600
Why are you here?

68
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:51,160
Weren't you having fun?

69
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:53,600
I was, but...

70
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,080
I quit the club early on.

71
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,500
So celebrating with them like that...

72
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,760
Kind of feels like I'm out of place, you know?

73
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:02,720
What are you doing here in a place like karaoke?

74
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:06,700
Should I pretend it's all a coincidence?

75
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:10,100
No, me coming to karaoke alone is weird too!

76
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:10,500
Huh?

77
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,300
Did you maybe...

78
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:18,720
Follow me here?

79
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:19,500
Huh?

80
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:20,940
Huh?

81
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:21,540
What?

82
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,940
No, I, uh...

83
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,400
I, um...

84
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:26,200
Wasn't worried about you or anything.

85
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,200
Ah!

86
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,080
Ichikawa...

87
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:33,900
Huh?

88
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:39,960
Did you maybe hear me say I liked someone when we were in the nurse's office the other day?

89
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:40,920
Huh?

90
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,220
Huh?

91
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:45,700
Well...

92
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,320
Now?

93
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,240
Well, it's...

94
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,300
Just...

95
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:52,240
When I was saying it out loud...

96
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,540
My heart started racing like crazy.

97
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,120
Kind of...

98
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:58,240
Like I was realizing it all over again.

99
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,160
And so I got worked up!

100
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:02,680
Which had me acting like a weirdo all day long.

101
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:02,780
Huh?

102
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:06,700
I'm sorry.

103
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,800
It doesn't make sense, huh?

104
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:12,280
But that's all it is, so you don't need to worry about it at all.

105
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,740
I mean...

106
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:15,660
That's not it.

107
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:17,360
I wasn't worried about that.

108
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:17,720
Huh?

109
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,460
Confront yourself.

110
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,640
And how creepy you are!

111
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:27,240
I didn't like seeing you go out with the b-ball guys.

112
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,520
I got all worked up, so...

113
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:29,700
Huh?

114
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:35,060
Sorry.

115
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:56,440
How did...

116
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,380
This even happen?!

117
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:28,360
Thank you.

118
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:33,990
Yesterday was such a mess.

119
00:07:33,990 --> 00:07:36,990
That's those basketball kids for you, extroverts.

120
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,990
They know no mercy.

121
00:07:42,990 --> 00:07:46,990
Uh, let's give it up for Ichikawa's great speech and singing voice.

122
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:49,990
Yeah, hooray!

123
00:07:49,990 --> 00:07:52,990
I mean, I guess they weren't all that bad.

124
00:07:52,990 --> 00:07:54,990
Ah, Ichikawa!

125
00:07:54,990 --> 00:07:56,990
Glad I found you.

126
00:07:56,990 --> 00:07:58,990
Hm? What's up?

127
00:07:58,990 --> 00:08:02,990
Well, it's just that there's something I want to talk to you about.

128
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:05,990
W-what's going on?

129
00:08:05,990 --> 00:08:06,990
What the-

130
00:08:07,990 --> 00:08:08,990
You were in here?

131
00:08:08,990 --> 00:08:10,990
Oh, you too, Yamada.

132
00:08:11,990 --> 00:08:14,990
Wait, Sweet Paradise? Count me super in!

133
00:08:14,990 --> 00:08:16,990
That's a relief.

134
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:20,990
Oh, and also, would it be alright if Kanzuki joins in with us?

135
00:08:20,990 --> 00:08:22,990
Wait, you mean like-

136
00:08:22,990 --> 00:08:26,990
In perfect sync.

137
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:31,990
Uh, but, um, wouldn't we just be in the way between you and Kanzuki?

138
00:08:31,990 --> 00:08:33,990
If it's like a date and all.

139
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:39,990
Well, um, I don't really get why, but he was the one who suggested that you two come along with us.

140
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:40,990
Hm?

141
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:41,990
Hm?

142
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:42,990
Why would he?

143
00:08:42,990 --> 00:08:43,990
Not sure.

144
00:08:43,990 --> 00:08:46,990
But truth is, the two of us go out alone plenty already.

145
00:08:46,990 --> 00:08:48,990
When did that guy start?

146
00:08:48,990 --> 00:08:50,990
Oh, okay.

147
00:08:50,990 --> 00:08:52,990
Well, just so we're clear and all.

148
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,990
Are the two of you going out as a couple?

149
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:56,990
No, not at all.

150
00:08:56,990 --> 00:09:00,990
You go out together all the time, but you're still not going out as a couple?

151
00:09:00,990 --> 00:09:01,990
What?

152
00:09:01,990 --> 00:09:02,990
Hm.

153
00:09:02,990 --> 00:09:03,990
What?

154
00:09:03,990 --> 00:09:05,990
I don't mind if you don't.

155
00:09:05,990 --> 00:09:06,990
It sounds like it'll be fun.

156
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:09,990
If she gets in the way too much, you can just ditch her.

157
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:10,990
Huh?

158
00:09:10,990 --> 00:09:11,990
Oh.

159
00:09:11,990 --> 00:09:12,990
Well, you're coming too.

160
00:09:12,990 --> 00:09:13,990
Huh?

161
00:09:13,990 --> 00:09:18,990
I mean, this Saturday is March 14th, you get it?

162
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:23,990
White day!

163
00:09:23,990 --> 00:09:25,990
I'll go if I can.

164
00:09:25,990 --> 00:09:26,990
That means you will!

165
00:09:26,990 --> 00:09:27,990
Does it really?

166
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:28,990
But...

167
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:31,990
She says she'll come.

168
00:09:31,990 --> 00:09:34,990
Oh, that's great to hear.

169
00:09:34,990 --> 00:09:36,990
And you too.

170
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:37,990
Huh?

171
00:09:38,990 --> 00:09:40,990
Does that make this...

172
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:42,990
A double date?

173
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,990
This'll be fun.

174
00:09:52,990 --> 00:09:54,990
Today's the big day.

175
00:09:54,990 --> 00:09:56,990
Here as fast as always.

176
00:09:56,990 --> 00:09:57,990
Ichikawa!

177
00:10:01,990 --> 00:10:02,990
Ugh.

178
00:10:02,990 --> 00:10:03,990
Not in her uniform.

179
00:10:03,990 --> 00:10:05,990
Took the same train, huh?

180
00:10:05,990 --> 00:10:09,990
It's still a little early, so I thought I might be waiting alone.

181
00:10:09,990 --> 00:10:10,990
Oh, yeah.

182
00:10:10,990 --> 00:10:13,990
I thought I'd get some shopping in beforehand.

183
00:10:13,990 --> 00:10:15,990
For white day, you mean?

184
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:16,990
Um, what?

185
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:17,990
No.

186
00:10:17,990 --> 00:10:18,990
Nothing like that, really.

187
00:10:18,990 --> 00:10:22,990
Truth is, I still can't make up my mind about it.

188
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,990
Let me see if I can help.

189
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:26,990
This is Yamada we're talking about.

190
00:10:26,990 --> 00:10:27,990
Exactly.

191
00:10:28,990 --> 00:10:29,990
I knew it.

192
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:31,990
How does she know?

193
00:10:32,990 --> 00:10:34,990
I guess it's fine if it's just her.

194
00:10:35,990 --> 00:10:37,990
The more I think about it, the more I can't decide.

195
00:10:38,990 --> 00:10:39,990
I'm so lost about it.

196
00:10:39,990 --> 00:10:42,990
All I can find online is what not to get.

197
00:10:42,990 --> 00:10:43,990
I know what you mean.

198
00:10:43,990 --> 00:10:47,990
I can't promise I'll be a huge help or anything.

199
00:10:47,990 --> 00:10:49,990
But wanna go shopping together?

200
00:10:49,990 --> 00:10:50,990
Huh?

201
00:10:50,990 --> 00:10:51,990
Wait, but can we...

202
00:10:51,990 --> 00:10:52,990
We're here.

203
00:10:52,990 --> 00:11:05,990
Is this whole situation really okay?

204
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:08,990
You probably can't go wrong with food as a gift.

205
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:12,990
It's just, she eats nothing but delicious stuff all the time.

206
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:13,990
Yeah, that's true.

207
00:11:13,990 --> 00:11:16,990
And it'd be so weird if I made something for her, right?

208
00:11:16,990 --> 00:11:18,990
She would probably think I poisoned it.

209
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:19,990
Seriously?

210
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:21,990
I wouldn't say that.

211
00:11:21,990 --> 00:11:24,990
What was it that she gave you on Valentine's Day?

212
00:11:24,990 --> 00:11:27,990
Um, like a chocolate muffin or something?

213
00:11:27,990 --> 00:11:28,990
A handmade one?

214
00:11:28,990 --> 00:11:29,990
Yeah.

215
00:11:30,990 --> 00:11:31,990
What did you think?

216
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:32,990
What?

217
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:34,990
I mean, well I was pretty happy.

218
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:38,990
But there's a difference between something she makes and something I make.

219
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:39,990
You think so?

220
00:11:43,990 --> 00:11:46,990
Wouldn't buying jewelry be super weird and personal?

221
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:47,990
Ugh.

222
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:50,990
People do have their preferences.

223
00:11:50,990 --> 00:11:51,990
Ugh.

224
00:11:51,990 --> 00:11:56,990
Maybe I'll just give her a catalog to choose from.

225
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:59,990
That's a little impersonal, don't you think?

226
00:11:59,990 --> 00:12:00,990
Ugh.

227
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:01,990
Ugh.

228
00:12:01,990 --> 00:12:04,990
I'm being pretty negative, aren't I?

229
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:05,990
Sorry.

230
00:12:05,990 --> 00:12:07,990
I get it.

231
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:09,990
I'm kinda the same way.

232
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:13,990
Guess we're a bit similar in that way, aren't we?

233
00:12:13,990 --> 00:12:14,990
Huh?

234
00:12:14,990 --> 00:12:15,990
What's that mean?

235
00:12:15,990 --> 00:12:16,990
She's scaring me!

236
00:12:16,990 --> 00:12:17,990
Ugh.

237
00:12:25,990 --> 00:12:26,990
How about a hat?

238
00:12:26,990 --> 00:12:28,990
A fluffy hat for Yamada.

239
00:12:28,990 --> 00:12:29,990
Ichika!

240
00:12:29,990 --> 00:12:30,990
Oh yeah!

241
00:12:30,990 --> 00:12:31,990
That would look cute!

242
00:12:31,990 --> 00:12:32,990
Huh?

243
00:12:32,990 --> 00:12:33,990
Huh?

244
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:34,990
Huh?

245
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:35,990
Huh?

246
00:12:35,990 --> 00:12:36,990
What?

247
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:37,990
Oh yeah!

248
00:12:37,990 --> 00:12:38,990
That would totally look cute!

249
00:12:38,990 --> 00:12:40,990
You do look super adorable!

250
00:12:40,990 --> 00:12:41,990
Right?

251
00:12:41,990 --> 00:12:42,990
Is this...

252
00:12:42,990 --> 00:12:43,990
Chelsea?

253
00:12:43,990 --> 00:12:44,990
Huh?

254
00:12:44,990 --> 00:12:48,990
Oh dude, it's not like what you're thinking at all!

255
00:12:48,990 --> 00:12:49,990
Wait a minute...

256
00:12:49,990 --> 00:12:50,990
Why is he here early?

257
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:52,990
Yamada, you look super cute as always, too!

258
00:12:52,990 --> 00:12:54,990
Isn't that right?

259
00:12:54,990 --> 00:12:55,990
Huh?

260
00:12:55,990 --> 00:12:56,990
She looks real cute!

261
00:12:56,990 --> 00:12:57,990
Right?

262
00:12:57,990 --> 00:12:58,990
Yeah!

263
00:12:58,990 --> 00:12:59,990
Yeah!

264
00:12:59,990 --> 00:13:00,990
Totally!

265
00:13:00,990 --> 00:13:01,990
Hara!

266
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:02,990
Well, it's almost time to eat!

267
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:18,990
So we should all get going then!

268
00:13:18,990 --> 00:13:22,990
This is dumb!

269
00:13:22,990 --> 00:13:24,750
This is dumb.

270
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:26,910
Everyone's got things all mixed up.

271
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:32,390
Think I'll take one of these too.

272
00:13:32,390 --> 00:13:34,050
I can't decide.

273
00:13:36,070 --> 00:13:38,150
Hara's so adorable, isn't she?

274
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:38,990
Sure thing.

275
00:13:38,990 --> 00:13:40,230
Don't you go agreeing!

276
00:13:40,230 --> 00:13:41,070
Huh?

277
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:43,110
You should say, I bet she turns you on.

278
00:13:43,110 --> 00:13:44,590
Now say it back to me.

279
00:13:46,430 --> 00:13:48,550
Hara really turns you on, huh?

280
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:50,770
Quit looking at her like that, creep.

281
00:13:50,770 --> 00:13:51,650
What?

282
00:13:51,650 --> 00:13:52,510
Better.

283
00:13:52,990 --> 00:13:55,310
Can I leave yet?

284
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:56,710
This is ridiculous.

285
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:59,450
I wasn't saying Hara looked cute.

286
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:00,530
Sorry for the wait.

287
00:14:03,390 --> 00:14:06,510
Hara, I'm paying for this, so eat all the dessert you want.

288
00:14:06,510 --> 00:14:07,270
You are?

289
00:14:07,270 --> 00:14:08,510
No, no, it's fine.

290
00:14:08,510 --> 00:14:09,870
I'm actually pretty full.

291
00:14:13,710 --> 00:14:16,310
Like a rumble from the Earth itself.

292
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,870
She's always like this.

293
00:14:17,870 --> 00:14:19,910
That's why I invited Yamada.

294
00:14:19,910 --> 00:14:22,650
I just figured if she was here, then Hara would feel free

295
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:24,970
to eat as much food as she liked.

296
00:14:24,970 --> 00:14:26,370
Oh, yeah.

297
00:14:26,370 --> 00:14:28,610
You're perfect enough just the way you are.

298
00:14:28,610 --> 00:14:29,110
Nothing's better.

299
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:32,610
